This project builds on the following, and does not redistribute their toolchains:
- Bend (https://bend-lang.com), used as a proof backend.
- Lean 4 (https://lean-lang.org), Apache-2.0, used as a proof backend.
- Lasm (https://github.com/Millillion/lasm), MIT, which compiles Lean to WebAssembly.
- The Ghosts of Departed Proofs idea (Matt Noonan, 2018) and its TypeScript
  take, gdp-ts (https://github.com/rauchg/gdp-ts), which the gate follows.
None of these projects endorses this one.

examples/refunds/kernels/bend/refunds/refunds.mjs is JavaScript emitted by the
Bend compiler from the example's own Bend source, committed so the example
runs without Bend installed.

src/runtime/index.ts copies the Standard Schema interface (https://standardschema.dev),
as that specification allows.
